    {
      "id": "claim_775e45915bf34ed8a00303ab6faa4e12",
      "statement": "Self-issued one-time tokens and client-side dialogs are rejected as approval stand-ins because they sit on the same addressable surface as the method they guard, bypass the deployment's configured ask/never policy, and produce no approval audit; a confirmation only the guarded code can check confirms nothing.",
      "evidence": [
