    {
      "id": "claim_8f9d19f6b6cc4bf39d55ee8f63e5b504",
      "statement": "MemoService.readExternalPath reads external file text but is deliberately never decorated with @Remote: the capability is wanted while the confirmation point is absent, so nothing may reach it over the wire, and its method body carries no approval or permission check, which makes the missing wire name the entire boundary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/memo/dsh-memo/src/index.ts#L1591-L1624",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:722472863963da14b6095ce774fa2afd085bc81e32fdfc311fa965aead6f32f6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8a2038a806954e918b2b9df33f8269f3",
      "statement": "external-path.spec.ts pins the absence as the contract: it derives the endpoint list with remoteMethods(memo) and asserts addEntry is present while readExternalPath is absent, with that positive control keeping the assertion from silently becoming an empty shell; a missing method means the endpoint does not exist rather than being restricted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/memo/dsh-memo/tests/external-path.spec.ts#L98-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a60e0dcb2fd0eea39dd76d9019cbb211574da6a9afdf0aef621312ec43925e2e:"
        }
