    {
      "id": "claim_309e993d2b054a6684faa0e84f0362de",
      "statement": "The github-issue intake path realizes the turn-time shape without calling ctx.approval itself: the @Remote dispatchIssue and runIntake endpoints only create a Session through the sessionController and queue the issue prompt via agents.get(id).agent.followup, so the sensitive work happens inside that Session's agent turn; routing through the controller instead of ctx.agents.create() also keeps the deployment's preset, workspace and publish policy intact, which is what makes the dispatched Session behave like one the user opened.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/plans/2026-11-02-github-issue-intake-autopilot-design.md#L26-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1e3b18bbcf22c52edcc4ea3f20ce7a155c6daf48a9c9b88b57259bd88434b7ca:"
