      "statement": "The rule has documented history in this repository: the 2026-10-21 design document revoked a requirement that readExternalPath prompt a consent dialog before the client call, on the ground that the boundary never existed in code and no caller could implement it, and a one-time confirmation token was deferred as unverifiable at the time and is now excluded by the rule outright.",
